WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.600
Relatively little is known about one&nbsp;
of Tesla’s most powerful executives.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.380
Tom Zhu was Tesla’s chief in&nbsp;
China and the Asia region,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.920
and he led the construction and&nbsp;
operation of Gigafactory Shanghai.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.740
He’s been so impressive that in April 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:21.180
Elon gave him a huge promotion, to&nbsp;
senior vice president of automotive.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.360
Where he’s responsible for&nbsp;
overseeing operations worldwide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.360
including all of Tesla’s assembly plants.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.580
This makes Zhu the highest-profile executive&nbsp;
after Elon Musk, according to Reuters, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.720
reports that those answering to Zhu include:&nbsp;
the director of manufacturing at Giga Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.700
the senior director of vehicle operations and&nbsp;
manufacturing engineering at the Fremont factory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.060
the vice president in charge of&nbsp;
Europe, Middle East, and Africa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.820
and the VP of sales and service in North America.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.440
The 43-year-old, who hails from Beijing,&nbsp;
obtained a Bachelor of Commerce in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.340
Information Technology from the Auckland&nbsp;
University of Technology in New Zealand.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.300
He then moved on to work at engineering&nbsp;
consultancy Kaibo Engineering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.240
founded by a Duke University MBA classmate.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.420
The firm offers expertise to&nbsp;
Chinese contractors wanting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.760
to expand infrastructure projects overseas.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.620
While working for Kaibo in North Africa, he&nbsp;
was reportedly introduced to Cal Lankton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.280
the then director of Tesla’s&nbsp;
global EV charging infrastructure.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.960
Impressed by his work, Lankton hired&nbsp;
him to join Tesla in 2014, to build&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.120
out Tesla's supercharging network in China.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.560
Zhu has been responsible for Tesla’s&nbsp;
tremendous growth in that region.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.740
Giga Shanghai went from a bare field in&nbsp;
January 2019 to a fully built factory in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.000
just nine months and delivered its first&nbsp;
vehicle in December of the same year.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.080
That’s despite battling typhoons&nbsp;
that hit the plant’s drainage system.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.340
Zhu and other Tesla employees took&nbsp;
matters into their own hands and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.640
went up to the roof to manually&nbsp;
drain the water with buckets.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:57.120
Wu Wa, who documents the development of&nbsp;
Tesla’s Shanghai plant on his YouTube&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.240
channel, posted footage showing&nbsp;
the aftermath of the destruction.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.260
Zhu played a significant role in&nbsp;
the quick recovery of the Shanghai&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:08.520
factory after COVID lockdowns in China&nbsp;
halted production for many companies.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.520
And when a COVID surge led&nbsp;
to a two-month lockdown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.740
Zhu is reported to have slept in the factory&nbsp;
the entire time, safeguarding its operations.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:22.500
On the rare occasion when he isn't at the factory,&nbsp;
Zhu resides in a two-bedroom public rental housing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:28.980
unit a 10-minute drive from Giga Shanghai and&nbsp;
costs less than 2000 yuan, or $280, a month.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:32.640
According to Chinese media, Zhu’s&nbsp;
parents have come to stay with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.720
He keeps his private life private but&nbsp;
we do know he also has a young son.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.520
Interestingly, the apartment complex is a&nbsp;
residential area for other Tesla employees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.600
which he revealed in an interview with&nbsp;
the Chinese car review website, PCAuto.&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.940
“It’s a great atmosphere. Say,&nbsp;
you help me get my parcel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.600
I get something for you. It’s a&nbsp;
good way of working and living.”

00:02:54.600 --> 00:03:00.480
He says he carpools with employees to the&nbsp;
Gigafactory and starts work at 6 or 7 am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.260
in order to catch his colleagues in North&nbsp;
America before they head home for the day.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.680
That includes communicating&nbsp;
directly with Elon Musk.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.100
He spends the rest of his time on&nbsp;
the production line, talking with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:15.420
engineers to solve technical problems,&nbsp;
and often doesn’t log off until midnight.&nbsp;

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.960
On his Chinese social media&nbsp;
account Weibo, he posted this:&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.860
“I wanna sleep so much, but the&nbsp;
job is so damn interesting.”

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.440
Zhu’s hard work has paid off.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.800
He’s made Giga Shanghai&nbsp;
Tesla’s most efficient factory.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.860
Its annual production capacity is over&nbsp;
750,000 vehicles which was more than half&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:40.020
of Tesla’s entire global production&nbsp;
of 1.37 million vehicles in 2022.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:44.460
Giga Shanghai can currently produce&nbsp;
one vehicle in less than 2 minutes!

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.060
That’s still not good enough. Zhu says the goal is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:52.080
to have a Tesla rolling off the&nbsp;
assembly line every 45 seconds.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.540
Shanghai achieved its productivity by designing&nbsp;
the factory in a straight-line layout,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.520
which simplifies the flow of materials through&nbsp;
the manufacturing process, increasing efficiency.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:08.580
It also has a robust in-house construction team to&nbsp;
avoid relying too much on third-party contractors.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:11.640
And the third factor is hard work.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:15.000
Thank you for being here late at night.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.480
Elon showed his appreciation&nbsp;
for Tesla’s China team when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.740
visited the country for the first&nbsp;
time in three years, in May 2023.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:30.480
“I tell people throughout the world&nbsp;
the cars we produce here are not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:34.620
the most efficient production&nbsp;
but also the highest quality.”

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:40.500
I would like to congratulate you&nbsp;
on the amazing work that you’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.560
done. It’s been incredibly impressive how you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.500
have been able to overcome so many difficulties&nbsp;
and challenges. It warms my heart to know.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.080
The Chinese government is a&nbsp;
strong supporter of Tesla,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.160
which was the first foreign automaker&nbsp;
to open an independent factory in China.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:00.060
Usually, foreign carmakers must&nbsp;
team up with a Chinese partner.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.620
But some wonder if Tesla’s position&nbsp;
might be impacted by the escalating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.960
tensions between the United States and China.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:13.860
I think as long as we’re needed in this country,&nbsp;
I don’t see there (being) much of a risk of that.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:19.860
Zhu has big ambitions for Tesla to grow&nbsp;
even faster - in China and around the world.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.760
It took 12 years for Tesla&nbsp;
to build 1 million vehicles.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.980
1.5 years to build its second.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:28.350
11 months to build the third million

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:31.200
And only 7 months later, it built its fourth.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.440
So we’re getting better at it&nbsp;
faster. Exponential growth.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.840
In an interview with his alma mater Duke&nbsp;
University, he described himself as “tenacious”.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.440
For his tenacity, he’s been handsomely rewarded.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:50.280
Recently acquiring an additional 339,060&nbsp;
shares in TSLA, according to an SEC filing.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:56.769
Given a share price of $214 when this video&nbsp;
was produced, they’re worth around $70 million.

00:05:56.769 --> 00:05:56.820
Who knows how much they’ll be when he cashes out.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:00.720
But for Zhu, it doesn’t appear to&nbsp;
be about the money. But the mission.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.880
“Until all the cars on the road are&nbsp;
electric cars, we will not stop.”

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.500
